# agent.suite — the flows an AI operator can drive, in one world, in order.
#
# Run it with `--driver agent`: one simulation boots, the lab's operator on
# node1 performs each flow from its prompt.md, and the same oracles that judge
# the scripted runs judge these. The chain advances in place, so this is one
# series against one world rather than six separate builds.
#
# smoke is absent on purpose: it is a connectivity probe, not a flow anyone
# would ask an operator to perform, and it declares no agent driver.
# expel-node is last because it mutates two-nodes and nothing puts it back.
bootstrap-user-software-key
adopt-node
object-store
object-store-peer
read-remote-peer
expel-node
